<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijayabahu III of Dambadeniya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1232–1236</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijayabahu III of Dambadeniya was a Sinhalese king who founded a new royal line after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a> to the invader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga-magha">Kalinga Magha</a>. He established himself at the rock fortress of Dambadeniya in the island's wet zone and recovered the Tooth Relic, making Dambadeniya the first of the south-western Sinhalese capitals.</p></div>
